## Phase 2 - Neural Networks from First Principles into PyTorch

**Libraries:** PyTorch

Build a micrograd-style scalar autograd engine, a tiny MLP trained with it, and a manual training loop. Then rebuild in PyTorch: tensors, `nn.Module`, `Dataset`/`DataLoader`, optimizers, checkpoints, CUDA device placement.

**Gates:** gradient check (hand-computed vs autograd), loss curve shows learning, overfit a tiny batch, explain forward/backward/optimizer step without notes.

---

## Phase 3 - Transformer Internals before Hugging Face Abstraction

**Libraries:** PyTorch, then Transformers/Datasets

The keystone correction to the original plan. Build tokenization, token and positional embeddings, scaled dot-product attention, multi-head attention, the full transformer block, and a tiny GPT-style model trained on a small corpus (nanoGPT scale, runs on the Legion 7). Add a generation loop.

Then, and only then, the Hugging Face text-classification project, where `Trainer` becomes a convenience you can see through rather than an oracle.

**Gates:** explain Q/K/V without notes, trace tensor shapes through attention, overfit a tiny text sample, map what `Trainer` does underneath.

