## Phase 5 - Local Inference and Model Serving

**Tools:** llama.cpp, vLLM, ONNX Runtime, OpenAI-compatible APIs

Local track (Legion 7 / RTX 5080 16GB): llama.cpp, GGUF, quantization ladder (Q4/Q5/Q8) measured against the Phase 4 eval set, appliance-realism constraints.

Cloud track (DigitalOcean): vLLM serving tests per the compute policy below, latency / tokens-per-sec / memory / concurrency benchmarks, OpenAI-compatible endpoints. Reuse Phase 4 prompts as the benchmark workload and serve the Phase 1 ONNX model through the runtime path.

**Deliverable:** written deployment recommendation mapped to the Sailfish delivery spectrum (local binary to hosted).

---

## Phase 6 - Fine-tuning, Deferred and Compressed

**Libraries:** PEFT, Transformers, Datasets, Accelerate

LoRA/QLoRA adapter on a small instruct model, 100-1,000 examples, before/after evaluation on a held-out set, compared against the non-fine-tuned prompting/RAG baseline. Prior QLoRA exposure makes this consolidation, not new territory.

Order of value for small-business tooling: workflow design, retrieval, evaluation, prompting/tool use, model/runtime choice, and only then fine-tuning. The deliverable is an evidence-based "was it worth it" decision memo.

**TRL/DPO:** off the main path. Optional advanced module only if a concrete need appears (answer-style ranking, refusal behavior, domain response quality).

