## Compute Policy

**Provider:** DigitalOcean (committed; all infrastructure already lives there). RunPod is fallback only, for disposable short experiments if DO pricing or availability is inefficient.

### The Three-rung Ladder

| Rung | Hardware | Rate | Role |
|------|----------|------|------|
| 1 | Legion 7 / RTX 5080 16GB (local) | n/a | llama.cpp, GGUF quantization, appliance realism, small embedding/RAG tests, tiny-GPT training |
| 2 | DO RTX 4000 Ada 20GB | ~$0.76/GPU/hr | vLLM smoke tests, small-model serving |
| 3 | DO RTX 6000 Ada or L40S 48GB | ~$1.57/GPU/hr | Default serious cloud serving target; 7-14B with headroom, heavier RAG benchmarks, Phase 6 fine-tuning if VRAM-constrained |

**H100 (~$3.39/hr) requires written justification** (realistically only a high-concurrency benchmark). **H200 and MI300X are off the table**: nothing in Phases 5-6 needs the memory, and MI300X means ROCm friction that teaches nothing transferable.

Rates are current as of 2026-07-06 and must be rechecked before provisioning.

### Operational Rule

> [!warning] Create, benchmark, save artifacts, destroy. Never merely power off.
> DO bills powered-off GPU Droplets because disk, CPU, RAM, IP, and GPU capacity stay allocated. Billing ends only on destroy. The Phase 0 provisioning script makes this automatic, not a discipline problem.

