## Publication Filter

Working notes stay internal by default. **At each phase boundary** (not continuously; polish-drift mid-phase is the failure mode), run the phase's notes through the filter and **promote at most one** to a published Cajun Data technical note.

A note is publication-worthy only if it does at least one of the following:

1. Demonstrates technical judgment relevant to Cajun Data / Sailfish
2. Explains a practical ML concept for small-business systems
3. Supports the local-first / Business Hub positioning
4. Could help attract a technical partner, launch partner, or sophisticated customer
5. Shows measured results, not just opinions

| Document type | Default bar | Publish? |
|---------------|-------------|----------|
| Error analysis | Internal working note | Case by case |
| Decision memo | Internal working note | Case by case |
| Explainer | Internal first, polish only if strong | Case by case |
| Benchmark report | Higher polish if positioning-relevant | Likely candidate |
| Capstone architecture memo | High polish | Likely publishable |

